    {
      "id": 9,
      "title": "Missing readings — not instrumented in §4",
      "type": "text",
      "pluginVersion": "11.0.0",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 24,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 6
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Unavailable with the specified metric catalog.** No missing-readings metric, expected reporting cadence, active-meter population or interval-level labels are defined. Aggregate ingest counters cannot identify missing readings, and duplicate/conflict/error events are not a missing-readings count. This panel deliberately has no PromQL query rather than inventing a metric or treating zero ingest traffic as evidence of missing intervals. A dedicated low-cardinality aggregate missing-readings metric (or an agreed recording rule with expected-arrival inputs) is required from the backend."
      }
    }
